  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Access to Medical Services in Khartoum and Emergency Medical Assistance in Darfur</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sudan continues to experience the world&apos;s largest internal displacement crisis, with over 9.5 million people currently displaced - many of them multiple times, making 1 in every 7 internally displaced persons (IDPs) worldwide Sudanese. Through this project, IOM is responding on two fronts: supporting urgent humanitarian needs in Darfur while supporting returnees in Khartoum. In Darfur, IOM is working to provide local implementing partners with sub-grants, managed through its Grants Management and Capacity Building (GMCB) Unit, to respond rapidly to the increasing health needs in the region through the deployment of healthcare workers to primary healthcare centres (PHCs) and through mobile clinics to lesser-accessible areas North Darfur state. In Khartoum, IOM is working through its Migration Health Unit to directly implement the activities and deploy one mobile clinic to serve dense population centres.</narrative>
  </description>
